Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 AUG 95 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II III  PRESENT THROUGHOUT ALL THREE SPECIMENS AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS IN ALL THREE SPECIMENS  WITH LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT THROUGHOUT ALL THREE SPECIMENS  3  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Lobular carcinoma in situ may also be present  Immunoperoxidase stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  09 AUG 95 at 16 25 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   are three fragments of breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  with rubbery  white bands and ill defined  firm areas  A firm area from the largest fragment is frozen and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes A through N  The largest fragment is in A G  the smaller fragments are in H J  and the remaining undesignated tissue is in K N  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
