Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a 20 x 20 x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  an axillary tail measuring 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and a strip of muscle measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The nipple is inverted with areas of nodularity around it  and there are two pink red bruises measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in greatest dimension over the skin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned into twelve slices from medial to lateral  and reveals a firm stellate mass  identified by a clip  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The mass is found towards the middle of the specimen in slices seven and eight  The closest deep margin is 3 5cm from the mass  and 2 5cm from the skin  One arm of the stellate mass extends inferiorly and towards the axillary tail forming a firm nodularity but no discrete mass  and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is found in slices eight and nine  This nodularity is 4 0cm from the black ink  There is a second  ill defined  stellate  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  which abuts the nipple and is found in slices five and six  This area is 3 0cm medial to the stellate mass identified by the clip and is 4 0cm from the black ink  The rest of the breast tissue consists of grossly unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is submitted as follows  A  Portion of stellate mass and closest black inked margin  B D  Further representative sections of the stellate mass  E  Nipple with mass abutting nipple  F and G  Further representative sections of lesion beneath nipple  H I  Representative sections of nodularity extending inferiorly and medially from scar  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail and submitted individually in cassettes J P  A large  possibly matted lymph node bisected and submitted in cassette Q and R  One lymph node bisected and now in S T  U  Six small lymph nodes submitted entirely  Most of the lymph nodes contain necrotic pasty material  V W  Grossly unremarkable breast tissue  NOTE  The tumor extensively involves lymphatic vessels  Definite stromal invasion is not seen  but micro invasion cannot be completely excluded  The margin of the specimen appears free of tumor  Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , No.
